* LM13700 operational transconductance amplifier, one of two (our model from the sheet)
* Built by Solum Builder from TI LM13700 data sheet SNOSBW2F (November 1999,
* revised November 2015), typical figures at 25 degC, +-15 V. Behavioural core:
* Iout = Iabc*tanh(Vd/2VT); bias pin two junctions to V-; linearising diodes and the
* Darlington buffer as junctions. The dual is two instances on shared vp/vn.
.subckt LM13700_OTA inp inn out iabc dbias bufin bufout vp vn
Vsense iabc ib0 0
Dbias ib0 vn DBIAS
* Iabc as a voltage (1 V per A) for the expressions
Bia ia 0 V=max(i(Vsense),0)
* input-pair window: the common-mode range
Bw w 0 V=((pwr(max(v(vp)-1.5-(0.5*(v(inp)+v(inn))),0),2)/(pwr(max(v(vp)-1.5-(0.5*(v(inp)+v(inn))),0),2)+0.0025))*(pwr(max((0.5*(v(inp)+v(inn)))-v(vn)-1.5,0),2)/(pwr(max((0.5*(v(inp)+v(inn)))-v(vn)-1.5,0),2)+0.0025)))
* the pair's halves I5 (to the output's source mirror) and I4 (to the sink), then the
* open-loop bandwidth pole (2 MHz) on each, in the mirrors (after the tanh,
* so a large step slews at Iabc/C instead of winding up a filtered input voltage)
Bi5 i5r 0 V=v(ia)*v(w)*0.5*(1+tanh((v(inp)-v(inn))/(2*(8.617333e-5*(temper+273.15)))))
Bi4 i4r 0 V=v(ia)*v(w)*0.5*(1-tanh((v(inp)-v(inn))/(2*(8.617333e-5*(temper+273.15)))))
R5 i5r i5 1k
C5 i5 0 7.95775e-11
R4 i4r i4 1k
C4 i4 0 7.95775e-11
* output: source from V+, sink to V-, each stopping at the swing limit; Early sets Rout
Bsrc vp out I=v(i5)*(pwr(max(v(vp)-0.8-v(out),0),2)/(pwr(max(v(vp)-0.8-v(out),0),2)+0.0025))*(1+max(v(vp)-v(out),0)/1503.96)
Bsnk out vn I=v(i4)*(pwr(max(v(out)-v(vn)-0.6,0),2)/(pwr(max(v(out)-v(vn)-0.6,0),2)+0.0025))*(1+max(v(out)-v(vn),0)/1503.96)
Cout out vn 4.75e-12
Rleak out vn 3e+11
Rleak2 out vp 3e+11
* input bias currents: the pair's base currents (unfiltered Vd), into the tail at V-
Bbp inp vn I=v(ia)*v(w)*0.5*(1+tanh((v(inp)-v(inn))/(2*(8.617333e-5*(temper+273.15)))))/(0.5*pwr(10,log10(min(max(v(ia),1e-7),1e-3)))/pwr(10,((0.041643)*log10(min(max(v(ia),1e-7),1e-3))+(1.24808))*log10(min(max(v(ia),1e-7),1e-3))+(-2.03586)))
Bbn inn vn I=v(ia)*v(w)*0.5*(1-tanh((v(inp)-v(inn))/(2*(8.617333e-5*(temper+273.15)))))/(0.5*pwr(10,log10(min(max(v(ia),1e-7),1e-3)))/pwr(10,((0.041643)*log10(min(max(v(ia),1e-7),1e-3))+(1.24808))*log10(min(max(v(ia),1e-7),1e-3))+(-2.03586)))
Rdiff inp inn 2.462e+11
Cinp inp vn 5.96e-12
Cinn inn vn 5.96e-12
* quiescent: V+ draws 2.6 x Iabc at balance (Iabc/2 of it is the output pair);
* none unpowered, so a V+ left open still solves (D-237)
Bq vp vn I=2.1*v(ia)*(pwr(max(v(vp)-v(vn),0),2)/(pwr(max(v(vp)-v(vn),0),2)+0.0025))
* linearising diodes D2 (to -input) and D3 (to +input), anodes on the diode-bias pin
D2 dbias inn DLIN
D3 dbias inp DLIN
* Darlington buffer Q12, Q13, collectors on V+
Q12 vp bufin q13b QBUF
Q13 vp q13b bufout QBUF
.model DBIAS D(IS=2.39893e-15 N=2.1709 RS=0)
.model DLIN D(IS=2.65763e-16 N=1)
.model QBUF NPN(IS=2.65763e-16 BF=104.3)
.ends LM13700_OTA
